<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29014" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mictŭālis</span></b> , e,
			adj.
		id. (only post 
		 class). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Relating to the passing of urine, wrinary</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">via,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cael.
						Aur. Tard. 5, 10, 91</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">viae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 5, 10, 121</span></i>
			.—Hence, <i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mictŭālis</span></b> ,
				is, f., <i>the urinary
				passage</i>, <i><span class="en">Cael. Aur. Tard. 5, 4,
			65</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>That promotes urine, diuretic</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">virtus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. Herb. 117</span></i>
			.— <i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mictŭāle</span></b> ,
			is, n., <i>a diuretic</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Cael. Aur. Tard. 5, 10, 122
		al.</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
